#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:3
msgid "Honeypot Class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:5
msgid ""
"The Honeypot Class makes it possible to determine when a Bot makes a "
"request to a CodeIgniter4 application, if it's enabled in "
"**app/Config/Filters.php** file. This is done by attaching form fields to"
" any form, and this form field is hidden from a human but accessible to a"
" Bot. When data is entered into the field, it's assumed the request is "
"coming from a Bot, and you can throw a ``HoneypotException``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:16
msgid "Enabling Honeypot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:18
msgid ""
"To enable a Honeypot, changes have to be made to the "
"**app/Config/Filters.php**. Just uncomment honeypot from the ``$globals``"
" array, like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:23
msgid ""
"A sample Honeypot filter is bundled, as **system/Filters/Honeypot.php**. "
"If it is not suitable, make your own at **app/Filters/Honeypot.php**, and"
" modify the ``$aliases`` in **app/Config/Filters.php** appropriately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:29
msgid "Customizing Honeypot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:31
msgid ""
"Honeypot can be customized. The fields below can be set either in "
"**app/Config/Honeypot.php** or in **.env**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:34
msgid ""
"``$hidden`` - ``true`` or ``false`` to control visibility of the honeypot"
" field; default is ``true``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:35
msgid ""
"``$label`` - HTML label for the honeypot field, default is ``'Fill This "
"Field'``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:36
msgid ""
"``$name`` - name of the HTML form field used for the template; default is"
" ``'honeypot'``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:37
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``$template`` - form field template used for the honeypot; default is "
"``'<label>{label}</label><input type=\"text\" name=\"{name}\" "
"value=\"\">'``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:38
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``$container`` - container tag for the template; default is ``'<div "
"style=\"display:none\">{template}</div>'``. If you enables CSP, you can "
"remove ``style=\"display:none\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/honeypot.rst:40
msgid ""
"``$containerId`` - [Since v4.3.0] this setting is used only when you "
"enable CSP. You can change the id attribute for the container tag; "
"default is ``'hpc'``"
msgstr ""

